00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:47.090
We still have not closed out the project.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:53.065
I thought we had closed it out or we were going to close it out about September.

00:11:53.385 --> 00:11:59.225
And then we kind of hit a snag with the state because the state wanted a material inspection form

00:11:59.385 --> 00:12:00.025
for

00:12:00.825 --> 00:12:09.760
one of the batches of rebar used in it. And they already had it, they just didn't know they had it. So that took about six months to go through the state system.

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:10.960
And

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:15.200
the bottom line is the bridge is done.

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:17.760
The state has given us authorization

00:12:18.335 --> 00:12:22.415
to close it out, but the problem is that the company

00:12:22.655 --> 00:12:23.615
surveyed

00:12:23.615 --> 00:12:27.135
it or that was our bridge representative,

00:12:27.215 --> 00:12:28.415
CME Engineering,

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.720
they disagree with the contractor

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:39.960
